{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2019-10-24 12:30:00', 'title': '3M SEES 2019 ORGANIC GROWTH IN CHINA DOWN MID-SINGLE DIGITS - CONF CALL', 'text': "3M CO EXPECTS ORGANIC GROWTH IN CHINA TO BE DOWN MID-SINGLE DIGITS IN 2019 - CONF CALL.3M CO SAYS WHILE SELLING PRICES WERE LOWER THAN EXPECTED IN Q3, CO’S SOURCING EFFORTS REDUCED RAW MATERIAL COST RESULTING IN A NET BENEFIT, WHICH IS EXPECT TO CONTINUE GOING FORWARD.3M CO SAYS RAISING EXPECTATIONS FOR 2019 FREE CASH FLOW CONVERSION TO A RANGE OF 105% TO 110% VERSUS 95% TO 105% PREVIOUSLY.3M CO SAYS CAPITAL EXPENDITURES REMAIN ON TRACK TO BE IN THE RANGE OF $1.6 BILLION TO $1.7 BILLION FOR THE YEAR.3M CO SAYS ANTICIPATE Q4 EPS IN THE RANGE OF $2.05 TO $2.15 AND AN ORGANIC SALES DECLINE OF 1% TO 3%.3M CO SAYS CO TESTIFIED BEFORE A CONGRESSIONAL SUBCOMMITTEE IN WASHINGTON IN SEPT. AND REMINDED THE COMMITTEE THAT SCIENTIFIC EVIDENCE DOES NOT SHOW PFAS CAUSING ADVERSE HUMAN HEALTH EFFECTS AT CURRENT OR HISTORICAL LEVELS.3M'S POSITION ON PFAS IS SHARED BY PUBLIC HEALTH AGENCIES AND INDEPENDENT SCIENCE REVIEW PANELS.3M SAYS CHANNEL RESPONSE TO DECLINE IN DEMAND IN AUTOMOTIVE AND ELECTRONICS MORE BROADLY TOOK PLACE IN H1 2019, BUT 3M SAW ADDITIONAL ADJUSTMENTS, A BIG PART OF THAT IN CHINA IN Q3.3M SAYS, ABSENT A RECESSION AND SOME OTHER MAJOR DOWNTURN IN THE MARKETS IN 2020, CO EXPECTS TO HAVE POSITIVE GROWTH ACROSS BUSINESSES.WITH RESPECT TO FOUR END MARKETS IN ELECTRONICS, 3M SAYS CONSUMER ELECTRONICS SAW SOFTNESS CONTINUE TO COME THROUGH IN Q3."}{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00', 'title': '3M SEES FY 2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.20 TO $8.30', 'text': '3M REPORTS THIRD-QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.72.Q3 SALES $8.0 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $8.16 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.49 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.99 TO $9.09 EXCLUDING ITEMS.SEES FY 2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.20 TO $8.30.SEES Q4 2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.05 TO $2.15.QTRLY ORGANIC LOCAL-CURRENCY SALES DECLINED 1.3 PERCENT YEAR-ON-YEAR.MACROECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT REMAINS CHALLENGING.CONTINUED TO EFFECTIVELY MANAGE COSTS AND REDUCE INVENTORY LEVELS.WHILE MACROECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT REMAINS CHALLENGING, WE EXECUTED WELL AND BUILT ON PROGRESS WE MADE IN Q2.FOREIGN CURRENCY TRANSLATION REDUCED SALES BY 1.3 PERCENT YEAR-ON-YEAR IN QUARTER.3M UPDATED ITS FULL-YEAR 2019 GAAP EARNINGS TO BE IN RANGE OF $8.20 TO $8.30 PER SHARE.3M ALSO UPDATED ITS FULL-YEAR ORGANIC LOCAL-CURRENCY SALES GUIDANCE TO DECLINE BETWEEN 1% TO 1.5%.QTRLY NET SALES FOR SAFETY AND INDUSTRIAL   SEGMENT OF $2,849 MILLION VERSUS $3,021 MILLION.FOURTH-QUARTER 2019 GAAP EARNINGS GUIDANCE INCLUDES AN ESTIMATED $0.15 PER SHARE NEGATIVE IMPACT FROM RECENTLY CLOSED ACQUISITION OF ACELITY.FOURTH-QUARTER ORGANIC LOCAL-CURRENCY SALES IS EXPECTED TO DECLINE BETWEEN 1 TO 3 PERCENT.EXCLUDING FULL-YEAR 2019 IMPACTS CO NOW EXPECTS ITS 2019 EARNINGS TO BE IN RANGE OF $8.99 TO $9.09 PER SHARE.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $9.29 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.41 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}